## Original Content
Illinois prosecutors shared defendants’ personal data with federal immigration agents without criminal warrants, public disclosure, or legislative oversight.

## Summary
Illinois county prosecutors illegally shared defendants' personal data with federal immigration agents without criminal warrants. This action was done without public disclosure or legislative oversight, raising significant privacy and legal concerns.

## Key Points
- Illinois prosecutors shared defendants' personal data with ICE agents.
- The data sharing occurred without criminal warrants.
- No public disclosure was made regarding the practice.
- There was no legislative oversight involved.
- This highlights issues in immigration enforcement and privacy rights.


